{"id":271326418127842,"type":"album","name":"Future Days","artist":"Can","year":1973,"weight":57,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710009.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-6a557839-2a65-43dd-822f-89df42420f19/mbid-6a557839-2a65-43dd-822f-89df42420f19-36773253857.jpg","label":"Mute","kind":"Album","tracks":4,"country":"XE","scaruffi":7.5,"aoty":86,"aoty_user":85,"yt":"wQxMB4Wk_y8","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/22ZgHorVJzcZ4m8YBZCw4w","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_kBxn-D-kRkzWpfSjJzHIZBbTsMepzm2IE","discogs":"https://www.discogs.com/release/6190798","bandcamp":"https://canofficial.bandcamp.com/album/future-days","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/can/future-days","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/aa41b178-9f16-3dc4-84b6-e9ad8b5be4b8","allmusic":"https://www.allmusic.com/album/mw0000653738","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/6045-can-future-days.php"},"desc":"Damo Suzuki's final effort is Can's most atmospheric and beautiful record, a spartan collection of lengthy, jazz-like compositions recorded with minimal vocal contributions. Employing keyboard washes to create a breezy, almost oceanic feel (indeed, two of the tracks are titled \"Spray\" and \"Bel Air\"), the mix buries Suzuki's voice to elevate drummer Jaki Liebezeit's complex rhythms to the foreground; despite the deceptive tranquility of its surface, Future Days is an intense work, bubbling with radical ideas and concepts. .","producers":"Can","engineers":"Andreas Torkler, Holger Czukay, Irmin Schmidt, Jono Podmore","credits":{"artwork [cover]":["Ingo Trauer","Richard J. Rudow"],"bass, recorded by":["Holger Czukay"],"composed by, written-by, producer":["Can"],"drums":["Jaki Liebezeit"],"guitar":["Michael Karoli"],"keyboards, other [alpha 77]":["Irmin Schmidt"],"lacquer cut by [vinyl cut]":["Kevin Metcalfe"],"photography":["Personal Can Archives"],"recorded by":["Chris Sladdin","Volker Liedtke"],"remastered by":["Andreas Torkl